Instead of generating an ISO that requires manual partitioning afterwards, this script creates a single, self-contained raw disk image (.img). It packs a bootable Live EFI system along with a pre-configured persistence partition baked right into the file—containing pre-generated SSH host keys, user authorized_keys, Wi-Fi configs, and the offline driver cache.
​You can dd this single .img file straight to a USB stick or run it directly inside a virtual machine (QEMU/KVM/Proxmox) as a ready-to-run "Mini Fog" live appliance.
​🏗️ Mini Fog Disk Layout (berry-mini-fog.img)

berry-mini-fog.img (Raw Bootable Disk Image)
├── Partition 1: EFI & Live OS (FAT32, ~2.5 GB)
│   ├── EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI + grubx64.efi
│   └── live/ (vmlinuz, initrd, filesystem.squashfs)
│
└── Partition 2: Pre-Baked Persistence (EXT4, ~1 GB)
    ├── persistence.conf ("/ union")
    ├── etc/
    │   ├── ssh/ (Pre-generated SSH Host Keys)
    │   └── berry-router/wifi.conf
    ├── root/
    │   └── .ssh/authorized_keys (Your SSH Public Keys)
    └── var/cache/berry-router/drivers/ (Pre-cached drivers)


